# Hash-locked tooling for the CodSpeed benchmark job ONLY.
#
# Regenerate: uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#   --python-version 3.10 \
#   --output-file=requirements-bench.lock requirements-bench.in
#
# Kept out of requirements-ci.lock deliberately, for the same reason as the
# fuzz and mutation locks: pytest-codspeed carries a compiled tracer and a
# `cffi` dependency that exactly one job on one OS needs, and adding it to the
# CI lock would install it on all fifteen matrix cells to be imported by none.
#
# The benchmark job installs this lock *next to* requirements-ci.lock (it needs
# pytest and the bridge's runtime dependencies to import `arena`), so the two
# resolutions have to agree on every package they share --
# scripts/lock_conflict_ratchet.py fails the build if they do not. The `-c`
# below is what keeps them agreeing when the lock is regenerated: uv reads the
# constraint out of the input file, so the plain `uv pip compile` the relock
# workflow runs resolves against the CI pins without anyone remembering a flag.
-c requirements-ci.lock

pytest-codspeed==5.0.3
